# A closed enum of quoted strings at the root — no object.
#
# ⚠️ Keep this fixture: it pins a real best-effort LIMITATION of
# grammar.root_object_keys, which scans the root RHS for `\"name\"` literals and
# cannot tell an enum VALUE from an object KEY. It therefore reports
# ["pass", "fail", "unknown"] here, and verify_conformance takes its object
# branch on a grammar that has no object. That is documented behaviour, not a
# bug to fix blind — the check is explicitly structural rather than a full GBNF
# parse. See freeform_string.gbnf for a root that genuinely reports no keys.
root ::= "\"pass\"" | "\"fail\"" | "\"unknown\""
